Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:36:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(desktop): sync desktop docs with plugin adoption,
 transcript, Wayland, update and GPU behaviour

Seven Desktop docs statements no longer match main:

- desktop-plugin-sdk.md: a marker-less desktop-plugins/<id>/ folder with a
  plugin.js was described only as a hand-installed standalone plugin.
  materializeDesktopHalf() now adopts such a folder in place (marker
  stamped, nothing else written) when its plugin.js byte-matches the
  package's own half, which recovers pre-marker installs (#112450).
- desktop.md, Reasoning Blocks: "(off shows answers only)" is false; the
  tool feed follows display.tool_progress, never show_reasoning
  (message-parts.tsx; use-hermes-config.test.ts pins the independence).
- desktop.md, Markdown line breaks: the transcript renderer applies
  remarkSoftBreaks, so a single newline in prose is a line break; it is not
  plain CommonMark soft-break handling.
- desktop.md, Linux/Wayland: wslgLaunchArgs() defaults the NVIDIA
  proprietary driver to --ozone-platform=x11 unless a hint/flag chooses
  otherwise (#126013); a wayland hint is honoured like an x11 one.
- multi-connection-desktop.md: "Update all instances" is not fully
  parallel; updateConnectionsBeforeLocal() settles remote/SSH updates
  before the local handoff.
- bot-screen.md: _make_run_env() (local terminal backend) also merges the
  Bot Desktop's published DISPLAY/XAUTHORITY/D-Bus env while the screen is
  up (#125830), not only cua-driver and headed-browser spawns.
- environment-variables.md: HERMES_DESKTOP_NVIDIA_SWIFTSHADER no longer
  overrides a 580.x driver-series list; the fallback is a behavioural probe
  that engages after a witnessed GPU-process death (#124255).
